Day 15: Stored Procedures & Functions in MySQL 8

Topic:
Stored Procedures & Functions in MySQL 8

Learning Objectives:

Understand what Stored Procedures and Functions are and why they are used
Learn the difference between a Stored Procedure and a User-Defined Function (UDF)
Master CREATE PROCEDURE syntax with IN, OUT, and INOUT parameters
Learn how to create User-Defined Functions and understand their return behavior
Understand the CALL syntax to invoke stored procedures
Apply concepts through real-world use cases like salary increment and age calculation

Activities / Deliverables:

Read about Stored Procedures and Functions in MySQL 8 and prepare short notes
Write a Stored Procedure for employee salary increment using IN and OUT parameters
Write a User-Defined Function to calculate age from a date of birth
Test both using the CALL statement and SELECT in MySQL Workbench
Write a summary comparing when to use a Procedure vs a Function

Tools / Tech:

MySQL 8 (Database server)
MySQL Workbench (GUI tool for writing and executing procedures/functions)

